{"slug": "ken-homs-classic-kung-pao-chicken", "nyt_id": 11212, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11212-ken-homs-classic-kung-pao-chicken", "name": "Ken Hom's Classic Kung Pao Chicken", "author": "Alex Witchel", "description": "This recipe is adapted from the great Chinese-American chef Ken Hom, for a Sichuan stir-fry is made with chunks of boneless chicken (breasts or thighs, though we prefer thighs), peanuts, chile peppers and plenty of garlic, scallions and ginger. Making it is not at all difficult, but it does require one fussy step: The chicken takes a dip into a combination of egg white, salt, sesame oil and cornstarch before it goes into the hot wok. This step creates a lovely crust on the chicken that sears in moisture and later serves to hold onto the savory-sweet soy-sesame sauce. The dish is quite spicy, so serve it over rice or plain pasta to foil the heat, alongside an ice cold beer. Alex Witchel", "servings": {"text": "6 servings, with leftovers", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 25, "raw": {"total": "25 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 pounds boneless, skinless chicken breasts, cut into 1-inch cubes", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "boneless", "preparation": "skinless chicken breasts, cut into 1-inch cubes", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 large egg whites", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large egg whites", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 teaspoons salt", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 tablespoons Asian sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "asian sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 tablespoons cornstarch", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "cornstarch", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 cups peanut oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "peanut oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "6 dried red chiles", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "dried red chiles", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 ½ cups unsalted peanuts", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "unsalted peanuts", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "6 tablespoons minced garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup finely chopped scallions", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped scallions", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped fresh ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "⅓ cup chicken stock or canned chicken broth", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chicken stock or canned chicken broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "⅓ cup Shaoxing rice wine or dry sherry", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "shaoxing rice wine or dry sherry", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "5 tablespoons reduced sodium soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "reduced sodium soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "2 teaspoons sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "2 tablespoons Chinese black rice vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chinese black rice vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a medium bowl, combine chicken, egg whites, 1 teaspoon of the salt, 1 tablespoon of the sesame oil and 2 tablespoons of the cornstarch. Mix well."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Place a large wok over high heat until hot. Add peanut oil. When oil is very hot, remove wok from heat and immediately add chicken pieces, stirring to keep them from sticking. When the pieces are white on all sides, after 2 to 3 minutes, drain them and all the oil through a stainless-steel colander in a heatproof bowl. Reserve 5 tablespoons of the oil, and discard remainder."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a small bowl, combine remaining 1 tablespoon cornstarch with ⅓ cup water; mix well and set aside. Reheat wok with reserved oil. When very hot, add chiles and stir-fry until slightly blackened. Add peanuts, garlic, scallions and ginger, and stir-fry until lightly browned."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add chicken pieces, stock, rice wine, soy sauce, sugar, vinegar, remaining 1 teaspoon salt and remaining 2 tablespoons sesame oil. Mix well, and stir in cornstarch mixture. Stir-fry for 2 minutes, then reduce heat to low and let mixture sit for 2 to 3 minutes. Mix again, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 1572.4, "protein_g": 64.6, "carbohydrates_g": 17.0, "fat_g": 139.0, "saturated_fat_g": 22.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 166.0, "sodium_mg": 1078.8, "fiber_g": 3.8, "sugar_g": 4.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 107.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["chinese"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["chicken", "stir-fry"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/15/dining/Kung-Pao-Chicken/Kung-Pao-Chicken-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 1409}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2006-10-25", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:08:52.919560+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "ken-homs-grilled-soy-mustard-chicken", "nyt_id": 11320, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11320-ken-homs-grilled-soy-mustard-chicken", "name": "Ken Hom's Grilled Soy Mustard Chicken", "author": "Florence Fabricant", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "1 hour"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "12 skinless, boneless chicken thighs, about 1 ½ pounds", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "skinless", "preparation": "boneless chicken thighs, about 1 ½ pounds", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 tablespoons Japanese soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "japanese soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 tablespoons Dijon mustard", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "dijon mustard", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped fresh coriander", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh coriander", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped Italian parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped italian parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 tablespoon Chinese or Japanese sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chinese or japanese sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 tablespoon olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 teaspoons chopped orange zest", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "chopped orange zest", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 teaspoon chopped fresh ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "chopped fresh ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "With a sharp knife trim all the fat from the chicken. Place the pieces on a platter."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a blender or a small-capacity food processor mix the soy sauce, mustard, garlic, fresh coriander, parsley, sesame oil, olive oil, orange zest and ginger to make a rough paste. With a spatula spread this paste evenly over the surface of each chicken thigh. Cover with plastic wrap, refrigerate and marinate one and a half hours."}, {"position": 3, "text": "A half-hour before you are ready to grill the chicken, remove it from the refrigerator. Preheat a grill or broiler."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Grill the chicken, turning it once, until it is brown and fairly firm to the touch, 15 to 20 minutes total cooking time. Alternatively, the chicken can be broiled in a preheated oven broiler. Serve at once."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 302.7, "protein_g": 19.8, "carbohydrates_g": 1.9, "fat_g": 23.7, "saturated_fat_g": 5.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 111.1, "sodium_mg": 617.4, "fiber_g": 0.5, "sugar_g": 0.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 15.8, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["asian"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["chicken", "dijon mustard", "grill"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 73}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-05-02", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:14:09.270749+